      "id": 34,
      "statement": "audit-run.sh leaked its timeout watchdog because the EXIT/INT/TERM trap killed only the wrapping subshell, not the sleep blocked inside it. Killing a subshell does not signal its children. Fixed at fd0ebef: the watchdog sleeps in one-second slices, checks kill -0 on the parent each slice, and stays in the scripts own process group so group sweeps reach it",
      "evidence": "commit fd0ebef; tests/decision-events.bats now completes in 65s, was 1800s",
